From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akram-composio <akram@composio.dev>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:26:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] web: brand the web app as Kimono Photos

Why: Kimono hosts Immich as "Kimono Photos"; people should never see the Immich
name, flower or colours in the browser.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Every @immich/ui <Logo> (sidebar, auth, share, error, onboarding pages) and the
  `immichLogo` export show Kimono Photos' mark/lockup. Done by a Vite plugin in
  web/vite.config.ts (kimonoBrand) that redirects @immich/ui's own
  assets/immich-logo*.svg imports to web/src/lib/assets/kimono/*.svg (copied in
  by repatches branding/web/install.sh) and rewrites Logo.svelte's alt text. If
  @immich/ui renames its logo assets, update the plugin's regex, not call sites.
- Browser tab titles read "<page> - Kimono Photos" (root +layout.svelte,
  +layout.ts default meta, shared-link pages). No "Immich" in any <title>.
- PWA manifest name "Kimono Photos", short name "Photos", Kimono paper/plum colours.
  Favicons and app icons are replaced by branding/web (binary, not in this patch).
- The pre-boot stencil in app.html shows the Kimono Photos mark, static (no spin),
  and the <noscript> text names Kimono Photos.
- Auth pages are flat: AuthPageLayout no longer draws the giant blurred logo
  backdrop; its header shows the inline Kimono Photos lockup.
- Server-About modal and the generic server-error toast don't say "Immich".
- Colours, type and controls are the Kata theme patch's job ("web: dress the web
  app in Kimono's paper, ink and seals"), not this one.

